Short:        ReAction class rendering simple HTML 4
Author:       André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Uploader:     André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Type:         dev/gui
Version:      1.2
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, 68000+; htmlttf.gadget: RTG recommended
Distribution: Aminet

html.gadget and htmlttf.gadget are public ReAction (BOOPSI) gadget classes
for AmigaOS 3.2 that display simple HTML 4 documents - online help, readme
files, "about" pages, simple offline browsers.

Features
--------
 - headings, paragraphs, <pre>, <blockquote>, alignment, horizontal rules
 - text styles, <font size color face>, sub/superscript
 - lists (ul/ol with all numbering types, nested; dl)
 - tables with automatic column widths, colspan, rowspan, border,
   cellpadding, cellspacing, width in pixels or %, align/valign, bgcolor,
   captions, nested tables
 - links with visited/active colours, anchors, "#anchor" links handled
   by the gadget itself, link clicks reported as GADGETUP
 - pictures in every format a datatype exists for (GIF transparency, PNG
   alpha in htmlttf.gadget), scaled with width/height; with align=left/
   right the text flows around them (hspace, vspace, br clear)
 - background colours and tiled background pictures for the page, tables
   and cells
 - text selection with the mouse (drag, double click for a word) and
   copying to the clipboard (IFF FTXT)
 - Latin-1 entities, UTF-8 documents are converted automatically
 - scrollers connect via ICA_TARGET/ICA_MAP, mouse wheel and keys in the
   demo program

html.gadget uses the system's bitmap fonts and rounds bigger HTML font
sizes to sizes that really exist (e.g. Helvetica 9/11/13/15/18/24), so no
scaled bitmap fonts are shown. Rendering is flicker free through an
off-screen bitmap. Runs on every AmigaOS 3.2 system, 68000 and up.

htmlttf.gadget is a drop-in alternative with the same attributes that
renders anti-aliased TrueType fonts through a built-in FreeType 2.3.8
(Bitstream Vera included; DejaVu and Noto are supported as well),
composites everything in 32 bit (pictures with alpha channel) and
writes it with WritePixelArray() on RTG screens
or maps it to pens on palette screens.

Contents
--------
 Install              Installer script (English/German)
 Classes/Gadgets/     html.gadget, htmlttf.gadget (68000)
 Classes/Gadgets/68020/
                      htmlttf.gadget for 68020-68060 (Install picks it)
 Demo/                HTMLDemo (a small browser) with example pages;
                      "HTMLDemo TTF" uses htmlttf.gadget
 Developer/           includes (gadgets, proto, inline, clib), FD, SFD,
                      Autodocs
 Docs/                German documentation (LiesMich.txt)
 Icons/               the archive's icons as GlowIcons and NewIcons (and
                      the classic ones); double click UseGlowIcons,
                      UseNewIcons or UseClassic to switch
 Source/              complete source code (C, cross compiled with
                      bebbo's amiga-gcc and NDK 3.2; FreeType 2.3.8 from
                      Aminet dev/lib/freetype-2.3.8 is needed for
                      htmlttf.gadget)

The demo runs directly from the archive; to use the classes in your own
programs, run the Installer script or copy Classes/Gadgets/#? to
SYS:Classes/Gadgets/.

Not supported: CSS, JavaScript, frames, forms (drawn as boxes only),
text flowing around tables, network access.

History
-------
1.2 (04.10.2026)
 - printing and export: the new method HTMLM_Export writes the document
   as PostScript or PDF (paper size, margins, font size, Helvetica or
   Times, page numbers); text stays text, pictures with their original
   pixels and transparency, pages break between lines and keep headings
   with their text
 - bitmap printing: HTMLM_PrintBegin/Render/End give the pages as
   pixels of the sheet, in strips, e.g. for printer.device with
   DRPA_SourceHook; htmlttf.gadget in the printer's resolution,
   html.gadget with its bitmap fonts
 - HTMLDemo: export to RAM:HTMLDemo.ps / .pdf from the Project menu,
   bitmap printing through printer.device;
   it sets its own stack (32 KB), so it also runs without its icon
 - Autodocs and ReadMe: notes on the stack an application needs and how
   to set it in the code
1.1 (03.10.2026)
 - tables: cells spanning several rows (rowspan)
 - pictures with align=left/right, text flows around them
 - html.gadget: links are underlined with every font and without gaps
   between the words
 - list bullets are centred vertically in the line
 - htmlttf.gadget also as faster build for 68020-68060
 - icons also as GlowIcons and NewIcons (drawer Icons)
 - new demo pages: tables, text flow
 - HTMLDemo: no crash when started from the Workbench
 - checkboxes and radio buttons show their state, sized to the font
   (anti-aliased in htmlttf.gadget), e.g. for Markdown task lists
 - lists: type="none" on the list or an item hides the marker; a
   checkbox at the start of the item takes its place (task lists)
1.0 (30.09.2026)
 - first release

